/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Carbon monoxide is a colourless, odourless, poisonous gas.
   - φ is the equivalence ratio; F/A is the fuel–air ratio by mass. φ > 1 is rich, φ < 1 is lean.
   - In a petrol engine CO depends almost only on φ.
   - A diesel runs lean overall (φ about 0.3 to 0.8), so its engine-out CO is low.
   - Unburnt hydrocarbons are fuel molecules, and partly burnt pieces of them, that leave in the exhaust.
   - Some of the HC that leaves the crevices and the oil film burns in the hot gas during expansion and in the exhaust port.
   - NOx means nitric oxide (NO) plus nitrogen dioxide (NO2).
   - Zeldovich mechanism: O + N2 → NO + N, then N + O2 → NO + O.
   - Thermal NO therefore needs three things together: high temperature, oxygen atoms, and time at that temperature.
*/
