/* book exam traps: Saying NOx is highest in the richest, hottest-sounding mixture. NO peaks slightly lean, near φ = 0.9, because it needs spare oxygen as well as heat. | Writing “φ = 0.9 means an air–fuel ratio of 15”. For petrol, φ = 0.9 is 14.7 ÷ 0.9 = 16.3. | Calling three reactions “the Zeldovich mechanism”. The first two are the Zeldovich (thermal) mechanism; with N + OH → NO + H it is the extended Zeldovich mechanism. | Naming wall quenching as the main HC source. Crevices are the largest; the quench layer is only about 0.1 mm and much of it burns later. | Converting ppm to mass with the molar mass of NO when the rule asks for NOx as NO2: the answer comes out 30/46 of the right value. */
