/* book exam traps: Writing “smoke = particulate matter”. Smoke is the visible soot; PM also holds SOF, sulphate and ash, which can dominate at light load. | Treating the filter-sample volume as the engine’s exhaust flow. The filter sees diluted gas: multiply by the dilution ratio, then by the real exhaust flow. | Treating opacity, Bosch smoke number and filter smoke number as the same or as PM mass. They measure light extinction or paper blackening, mostly from soot, and use different scales. | Saying soot forms in the lean outer zone. It forms in the hot rich core and is burnt in the outer, oxygen-rich zone. | Assuming EGR always helps a diesel. It lowers NOx but raises PM. */
